WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.100
In the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, amen.

2
00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:09.180
Dear Jesus, may I enter into the eternal divine order of God

3
00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:13.720
to place my absolute nothingness in the heart of the Most Holy Trinity,

4
00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:17.980
to give to my God the joy of fulfilling the purpose of my existence

5
00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:22.800
by doing all the acts of my life through the immaculate heart of my mother, Mary,

6
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:25.400
and in the divine will of God.

7
00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:32.200
And in this same manner, may I live, pray, act, eat, walk, sleep, and do everything.

8
00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:36.600
May my soul be devoid of any other longings, wants, or desires;

9
00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:41.600
and may you, my beloved divine will, do with me whatever you want or desire.

10
00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:47.100
All I ask is that you bind me to your Most Holy Will so intimately

11
00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:51.500
that I may never swerve from carrying out what I know to be your good pleasure,

12
00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:55.300
and that I remain so docile to the movements of your divine will

13
00:00:55.300 --> 00:01:02.600
that you never perceive even a breath of resistance in my soul to your requests of me.

14
00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:07.700
Come divine will with all the angels and saints, especially my sweet mother, Mary,

15
00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:13.600
to touch my forehead, to imprint on it the Holy Spirit and infuse in me true light,

16
00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:20.000
so that I may understand the truths and the good that are in these writings and prayers, amen.

17
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:25.500
So, we want to begin this evening with January the 30th, 1926,

18
00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:31.500
and we begin with the announcement of the death of Father Francesco Devanadictis,

19
00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:33.700
who was Louisa's spiritual director.

20
00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:39.200
And we have this extraordinary situation that Louisa had been asking the Lord for years,

21
00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:44.700
that the confessor shouldn't have to really come round, that was really a thorn in her side.

22
00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:49.500
And then when she hears that instead, she goes into a bit of a crisis about it,

23
00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:51.500
which is very interesting.

24
00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:58.700
So, as she said, I was at the summit of my affliction because of the almost sudden death of my confessor,

25
00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:01.800
so it was absolutely not expected.

26
00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:06.500
To my many interior pains due to the frequent privations of my sweet Jesus,

27
00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:11.600
he wanted to add such a painful blow to my poor heart depriving me of the one

28
00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:15.000
who was the only person who knew my soul.

29
00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:19.600
Now, to be stuck in a bed with nowhere to go, as Louisa was,

30
00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:24.700
and to have somebody who actually understood her was an immense blessing.

31
00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:31.000
So, when it is taken away, it is huge to massive trial altogether.

32
00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:34.000
And if you think the Lord is going to be sympathetic,

33
00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:38.000
just wait for the rest of the message, it's just unbelievable.

34
00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:41.300
And again, it follows this thing that I've been telling you all the time,

35
00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:46.800
that the Lord allows her to go through a crisis, and then he explains why.

36
00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:50.500
And shows her what to do with it, and he's going to do this here as well.

37
00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:54.000
So, Jesus won't be sending her condolences or anything,

38
00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:57.400
but he will explain why this is happening.

39
00:02:57.400 --> 00:03:00.600
And you will realize that everything that happens to us,

40
00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:05.500
whether it's a bereavement or anything else, is all part of the divine plan,

41
00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:09.400
and it is the best thing for us, the people who have gone on,

42
00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:12.100
and the people who are left behind as well.

43
00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:15.300
And so, she rightly says, "Made the fiat velontas,

44
00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:19.300
to be always done, loved, and adored."

45
00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:21.900
The earth was now worded to possess such a person,

46
00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:24.700
which is a very high commendation of the priest,

47
00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:29.100
considering the relationship that Louisa herself has with the Lord.

48
00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:33.100
Therefore, the Lord to chastise us has brought him to heaven with himself.

49
00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:35.700
Now, that comment I find is very interesting,

50
00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:40.300
because Louisa has been asking the Lord for years to take her,

51
00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:43.200
and doesn't see that that might have been a chastisement for the rest of us.

52
00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:46.800
I mean, what would have happened to the whole divine will mission?

53
00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:51.500
So, in my intense bitterness for having been left without my confessor,

54
00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:55.800
not knowing myself to whom to turn, I prayed to my beloved Jesus

55
00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:58.700
for that blessed soul, and said,

56
00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:01.200
"And this prayer for him is really wonderful,

57
00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:04.300
and we should pray it for all the souls and purgatory."

58
00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:09.000
"My love, if you took him away from me, at least bring him straight to heaven with you,

59
00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:15.000
and crying, I said to him, 'I place him in your will.'

60
00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:19.900
We're being shown how to pray for the people who have gone on.

61
00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:21.900
Your will contains everything.

62
00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:27.500
It has love, light, beauty, all the good that has been done and will be done,

63
00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:31.700
and made these purify that soul that we're praying for,

64
00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:37.700
embellish him, enrich him with all that is needed in order to be in your presence,

65
00:04:37.700 --> 00:04:43.500
so that you will find nothing in him which might prevent his entrance into heaven.

66
00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:47.200
Every night, I prefer to pray that for all the souls and purgatory,

67
00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:49.000
so that they're all brought forward.

68
00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:52.700
I think it's the most wonderful prayer to pray for the dead.

69
00:04:52.700 --> 00:04:57.800
Now, while I was doing this and saying this, a globe of light came before me.

70
00:04:57.800 --> 00:05:04.400
Now, it's not often that Louisa actually says that a globe of light was put before her,

71
00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:07.700
and for those of you who have been in my classes previously,

72
00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:13.700
I have reminded you of Blessed Anna Maria Taige, who lived at the time of Napoleon,

73
00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:19.900
and she lived a very impoverished life just literally at the gates of the Vatican.

74
00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:23.700
And the Lord gave her the gift of a globe of light,

75
00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:31.200
and people from very high walks in life like cardinals and bishops and princes and kings and emperors

76
00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:34.900
and everything, they came to her for advice, and she would look into this,

77
00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:40.000
and the Lord would show her exactly what was to be said to the person.

78
00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:46.400
I remember just one case of this where a man of very high standing a layman came to her,

79
00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:52.900
and he was expecting the Lord to tell him he was going to have great success in the future,

80
00:05:52.900 --> 00:05:56.800
and the enterprises he was involved in was really great and all the rest of it.

81
00:05:56.800 --> 00:06:00.100
And Anna Maria looked at him and smiled and said,

82
00:06:00.100 --> 00:06:01.900
"I suggest you give up all of that."

83
00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:06.800
The Lord has told me to tell you to get ready to go, your time's up.

84
00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:10.400
I would imagine that had an absolutely unbelievable effect on him.

85
00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:13.100
This globe of light, his God is light.

86
00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:20.400
Sometimes he lets some of his favorites see in a way that the rest of us don't see.

87
00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:23.500
So this globe of light came before me, Louisa said,

88
00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:31.800
"And within that light, that is in the presence of God because God is light, one John, one five.

89
00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:33.900
There was the soul of my confessor."

90
00:06:33.900 --> 00:06:37.200
In other words, he was safe on the other side.

91
00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:43.500
He was with God, and he was making his way towards the vault of heavens.

92
00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:46.800
Now notice there is a journey on the other side,

93
00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:53.500
and since Jesus tells us in these writings that 9 out of 10 people who die go to purgatory,

94
00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:59.200
it means that the journey on the other side can be quite long.

95
00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:05.800
And that's why prayer for the souls in purgatory has to be very persevering.

96
00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:08.400
So he was making his way towards the vault of the heavens.

97
00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:10.500
Without saying even a word to me,

98
00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:13.200
he said, "I would imagine he was otherwise occupied."

99
00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:16.600
I remained consoled, yes, because of his destiny,

100
00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:19.400
but embittered the summit because of my own.

101
00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:23.600
And I prayed to Jesus that since he had taken the confessor away from me,

102
00:07:23.600 --> 00:07:26.500
that I myself had no one to whom to turn,

103
00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:30.500
by his goodness he would free me from the bother I gave to the confessor.

104
00:07:30.500 --> 00:07:36.200
Now she's kept this up for 18 volumes.

105
00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:40.100
This is really a thorn in her side she does not give up.

106
00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:42.600
And one of the things that fascinates me about Louisa

107
00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:45.200
is that if she gets something like this into her head,

108
00:07:45.200 --> 00:07:47.200
she doesn't let it go.

109
00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:51.800
She has this very deep relationship with the Lord.

110
00:07:51.800 --> 00:07:53.800
And yet she can hold on to something like this.

111
00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:55.100
It's very interesting.

112
00:07:55.100 --> 00:07:59.800
As long as we're on the earth, we're not complete.

113
00:07:59.800 --> 00:08:04.300
Or as I heard someone say, you're an unfinished symphony.

114
00:08:04.300 --> 00:08:10.300
When the last note was put in, then you're taken off.

115
00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:15.800
So here she is again saying that she didn't want the bother of having a confessor.

116
00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:19.100
I said it was Volume 1, it's really going on since Volume 2.

117
00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:22.600
However, not because it was wanted by me,

118
00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:24.500
but as something wanted by Jesus.

119
00:08:24.500 --> 00:08:27.400
Now this is the cleverest thing you ever came across.

120
00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:30.100
This is something she has wanted since Volume 2.

121
00:08:30.100 --> 00:08:32.200
And now she says to the Lord, but you know,

122
00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:37.300
what I want is that you will want it so that it's not just me that wants it.

123
00:08:37.300 --> 00:08:40.100
I think that's a bit of a convoluted way of going around it.

124
00:08:40.100 --> 00:08:44.100
Because I feel that if Jesus conceded this to me as something wanted by me,

125
00:08:44.100 --> 00:08:47.800
I would feel as if I were lacking the earth under my feet,

126
00:08:47.800 --> 00:08:50.800
the heavens above my head, and the heartbeat of my heart.

127
00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:52.300
Correct.

128
00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:54.700
You've gone back to square one.

129
00:08:54.700 --> 00:08:58.700
You wanted something so badly that you were insisting.

130
00:08:58.700 --> 00:09:01.600
So she actually sees the trap.

131
00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:05.200
Now whether this is put here for our benefit,

132
00:09:05.200 --> 00:09:06.900
well of course it's there for our benefit,

133
00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:11.500
but whether in its primal sense it's there for our benefit,

134
00:09:11.500 --> 00:09:19.000
I just wonder because human beings have this thing that we want to twist God's arm.

135
00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:21.200
And because it's God's arm, we can say, you know,

136
00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:23.300
God allowed it, God wanted it.

137
00:09:23.300 --> 00:09:29.400
So we have to be really careful that when we pray

138
00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:33.700
that we really are genuinely surrendering to God's will

139
00:09:33.700 --> 00:09:36.700
and that we're not trying to manipulate him.

140
00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:42.700
So from me, she said it would be a disgrace rather than a grace

141
00:09:42.700 --> 00:09:46.500
to manipulate God to try and get him to agree to do your will

142
00:09:46.500 --> 00:09:49.500
is a disgrace, not a grace.

143
00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:52.800
And so all abandoned in sorrow, I offered everything to Jesus.

144
00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:54.900
She realizes the trap that's there,

145
00:09:54.900 --> 00:09:58.400
that he would give me the grace to do his most holy will in every thing.

146
00:09:58.400 --> 00:09:59.800
See, that is the issue.

147
00:09:59.800 --> 00:10:02.300
It's very easy to write it on paper.

148
00:10:02.300 --> 00:10:08.400
It's very easy to say the words, but to actually do it in every single circumstance

149
00:10:08.400 --> 00:10:11.700
of our lives, that's a different subject.

150
00:10:11.700 --> 00:10:15.800
And for each one of us, we have different issues.

151
00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:18.700
And we might surrender on nine out of ten of them,

152
00:10:18.700 --> 00:10:20.800
but the tenth one is mine.

153
00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:22.600
That's what I'm holding on to.

154
00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:26.800
And so we can find ourselves struggling in areas that other people

155
00:10:26.800 --> 00:10:29.200
wouldn't even think about.

156
00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:32.800
But each one of us has an area, and this was Louise's one,

157
00:10:32.800 --> 00:10:38.000
that she did not want the confessor coming to bring her around every morning.

158
00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:41.000
And so Jesus sympathized with her in our sorrow,

159
00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:43.700
last her all to himself and said to her,

160
00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:47.300
"My daughter, courage, do not fear."

161
00:10:47.300 --> 00:10:50.100
Now notice how frequently he tells her not to fear,

162
00:10:50.100 --> 00:10:54.800
because I've told everybody, and I now notice I'm quoted all over the world for this,

163
00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:59.800
which is fascinating to me, that do not fear is in the Bible 365 times.

164
00:10:59.800 --> 00:11:03.600
You may not know where it originated, but it originated here.

165
00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:06.400
I'm fascinated that people just pick it up and quote it,

166
00:11:06.400 --> 00:11:10.500
but the frequency with which Jesus tells Louise not to fear

167
00:11:10.500 --> 00:11:12.500
is fascinating to me as well.

168
00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:14.300
So do not fear.

169
00:11:14.300 --> 00:11:15.600
I do not leave you.

170
00:11:15.600 --> 00:11:20.100
He's been telling her that since Volume 1, I do not leave you.

171
00:11:20.100 --> 00:11:24.000
That's Joshua 1, 5, if you have forgotten all the references

172
00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:26.500
I gave you in the early volumes.

173
00:11:26.500 --> 00:11:28.200
I will always be with you.

174
00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:31.000
Why? Because they are one.

175
00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:34.600
They've actually reached inseparable union.

176
00:11:34.600 --> 00:11:39.200
And I promise you that if no priest wants to make himself available for your assistance

177
00:11:39.200 --> 00:11:43.700
and he has explained to her that because of the role he has given to her

178
00:11:43.700 --> 00:11:48.400
as being the head of a new era in the history of the church,

179
00:11:48.400 --> 00:11:51.300
that he wanted his ministers to be present.

180
00:11:51.300 --> 00:11:54.700
The church had to be involved from the very beginning.

181
00:11:54.700 --> 00:11:59.000
She just seemed to have caught that idea.

182
00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:04.300
So if they don't want to make themselves available, not wanting to follow my will.

183
00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:08.500
Now, there is Jesus very carefully explaining to her

184
00:12:08.500 --> 00:12:12.800
that what she asked up above couldn't be his will.

185
00:12:12.800 --> 00:12:14.700
She asks that the priest no longer comes.

186
00:12:14.700 --> 00:12:17.700
She said, but I want it to be something that you want.

187
00:12:17.700 --> 00:12:21.900
And he said he very gently and carefully says to her,

188
00:12:21.900 --> 00:12:26.100
"If the priest doesn't want to assist you, he will not be doing my will

189
00:12:26.100 --> 00:12:29.400
because he's explained very clearly from volume two

190
00:12:29.400 --> 00:12:32.900
that it was his will that the priest would be involved."

191
00:12:32.900 --> 00:12:38.000
So if the priest should refuse, I will free you from this bother of having them,

192
00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:41.300
not because you wanted her because I myself wanted.

193
00:12:41.300 --> 00:12:47.200
And that would be because the church has refused, not because Louisa has asked.

194
00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:53.100
"Therefore, do not fear, for I will not let your will enter into this."

195
00:12:53.100 --> 00:12:59.700
This is very important, but he's very carefully go round to what she said.

196
00:12:59.700 --> 00:13:05.600
Why is he saying I will not let it because they have reached this inseparable stage?

197
00:13:05.600 --> 00:13:12.700
At the stage you and I are at, I presume we haven't reached inseparability in saying this.

198
00:13:12.700 --> 00:13:15.800
He wouldn't have this delicacy.

199
00:13:15.800 --> 00:13:19.800
I will not let your will enter into this, I will do everything myself.

200
00:13:19.800 --> 00:13:24.800
In other words, he will see to the priest, he will see to the need that is there,

201
00:13:24.800 --> 00:13:30.000
and he will see to Louisa being cared for by the church, everything.

202
00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:32.900
I will be jealous even of your breath.

203
00:13:32.900 --> 00:13:35.500
Now we've dealt with all of this in the early volumes.

204
00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:41.800
The jealousies of the Lord are very clearly expressed in Exodus numbers,

205
00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:46.800
just to give you three books of the Bible, but I'm not going to give you endless quotes out of them.

206
00:13:46.800 --> 00:13:50.300
And the Lord is jealous. Why would the Lord be jealous?

207
00:13:50.300 --> 00:13:53.800
It's because he is the creator of this person.

208
00:13:53.800 --> 00:13:58.300
He is the redeemer of this person. He is the ultimate goal of this person.

209
00:13:58.300 --> 00:14:03.300
This person cannot live without him. He is the Alpha and the Omega.

210
00:14:03.300 --> 00:14:07.800
Why wouldn't he be jealous of you giving your attention to something else?

211
00:14:07.800 --> 00:14:14.300
When he's the source of all your good, all your life, all your destiny, all your glory, everything.

212
00:14:14.300 --> 00:14:16.300
He's just everything.

213
00:14:16.300 --> 00:14:20.300
And so for someone in the position that Louisa is in,

214
00:14:20.300 --> 00:14:23.800
that she is to be the head of a new mission for him, a new generation,

215
00:14:23.800 --> 00:14:26.800
even her very breath. In other words, there's not to be.

216
00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:32.300
And it's expressed in that prayer we say before the reading and study.

217
00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:40.800
So that I will remain so docile to the movements of your holy will, that you will not perceive even a breath of resistance in my soul

218
00:14:40.800 --> 00:14:44.800
to your requests of me. That's what we're dealing with here.

219
00:14:44.800 --> 00:14:51.800
Not even a breath of resistance, not even a thought, a consideration, nothing.

220
00:14:51.800 --> 00:14:55.800
That your will may not enter into it, but only mine.

221
00:14:55.800 --> 00:15:04.300
Now, since he's making this complete demand, that absolutely everything is to be committed to him.

222
00:15:04.300 --> 00:15:06.300
He's going to explain why.

223
00:15:06.300 --> 00:15:11.300
So if you have your volumes beside you, what I do is I put headings on the paragraphs

224
00:15:11.300 --> 00:15:14.800
so that when I come back, I know exactly what I'm going to be reading.

225
00:15:14.800 --> 00:15:21.800
And the heading I would put on this paragraph is the destiny of the world is on Louisa's shoulders.

226
00:15:21.800 --> 00:15:27.300
That's why Jesus has to take care of every dot and tittle.

227
00:15:27.300 --> 00:15:33.300
